From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/colorop: Add the HLG inverse EOTF curve

A plane converted from SDR to an HLG output ends in BT.2100's HLG
inverse EOTF, the inverse OOTF and the OETF, for the 1000 cd/m^2
reference display BT.2408 maps SDR white onto. The fixed curves name
PQ's but no HLG one.

Add DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_HLG_INV_EOTF, "HLG Inverse EOTF": display
light in BT.2020 primaries, 1.0 the nominal peak, out to the HLG
signal. Its inverse OOTF weights each component by the luminance of
all three, which the curve's documentation states.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
  drivers/gpu/drm/drm_colorop.c |  1 +
  include/drm/drm_colorop.h     | 15 +++++++++++++++
  2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_colorop.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_colorop.c
index 682fcc651..953ab00a4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_colorop.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_colorop.c
@@ -79,6 +79,7 @@ static const char * const colorop_curve_1d_type_names[] = {
 	[DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_BT2020_OETF] = "BT.2020 OETF",
 	[DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_GAMMA22] = "Gamma 2.2",
 	[DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_GAMMA22_INV] = "Gamma 2.2 Inverse",
+	[DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_HLG_INV_EOTF] = "HLG Inverse EOTF",
 };
 
 static const struct drm_prop_enum_list drm_colorop_lut1d_interpolation_list[] = {
diff --git a/include/drm/drm_colorop.h b/include/drm/drm_colorop.h
index 224fae40e..842000ee9 100644
--- a/include/drm/drm_colorop.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_colorop.h
@@ -126,6 +126,21 @@ enum drm_colorop_curve_1d_type {
 	 * The inverse of &DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_GAMMA22
 	 */
 	DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_GAMMA22_INV,
+
+	/**
+	 * @DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_HLG_INV_EOTF:
+	 *
+	 * enum string "HLG Inverse EOTF"
+	 *
+	 * The Rec. ITU-R BT.2100-2 hybrid log-gamma (HLG) inverse EOTF for
+	 * the reference display: nominal peak 1000 cd/m^2, black 0, system
+	 * gamma 1.2. The input is display light in BT.2020 primaries, 1.0
+	 * the nominal peak. The inverse OOTF scales each component by
+	 * Y^(1/1.2 - 1), Y the BT.2100 luminance of all three, then the
+	 * HLG OETF encodes each. Represented by H.273
+	 * TransferCharacteristics code point 18.
+	 */
+	DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_HLG_INV_EOTF,
 	/**
 	 * @DRM_COLOROP_1D_CURVE_COUNT:
 	 *
